inline.body:
Confirmed and fixed in e512d3f61e. Reproduced the trace exactly: with `max: 500` over 1200 rows, after narrowing the filter off the selected rows the state is `allSelected: false, indeterminate: false` and `toggleAll()` selects 0 rows in the new view — an inert checkbox.

Went with your second suggestion: `toggleAll()` clears when the budget is spent. Treating a full budget as "all selected" would render the header checked while none of the visible rows are, which felt like the worse of the two lies — clearing also hands the budget back, so the next click selects within the narrowed view.

One thing worth calling out: I scoped this to the capped branch rather than making the `allSelected` branch clear too.

```ts
if (this.count() >= this.max) {
  this.clear();
} else if (this.allSelected()) {
  this.deselect(...this.selectable());
} else {
  this.select(...this.selectableWithinMax());
}
```

`clear()` and `deselect(...selectable())` diverge when the selection holds rows outside the current filter — `clear()` drops those too. That's the behavior you want at the cap (those held rows are what consumed the budget), but it would have been a silent semantic change for every uncapped table, so the uncapped path is byte-for-byte what it was.

Two regression tests added, verified they fail without the fix. 2132 green across libs/components, libs/vault, desktop, and web vault.

