inline.body:
⚠️ **IMPORTANT**: Rows selected past the cap window no longer make the header indeterminate.

<details>
<summary>Details and fix</summary>

`selectableWithinMax()` is `selectable().slice(0, max)`. With 600 rows in scope and `max: 500`, checking only row 550 leaves zero selected rows inside that window, so `indeterminate` is `false` and `allSelected` is `false` — the header checkbox renders completely empty while a row is visibly checked. Before this commit `indeterminate` measured against `selectable()` and correctly read as indeterminate here.

`allSelected` genuinely needs the bounded set (that was the point of the cap change); `indeterminate` doesn't — "some but not all" is well defined over the full in-scope set:

```ts
readonly indeterminate = computed(() => {
  const anySelected = this.selectable().some((row) => this.isSelected(row));
  return anySelected && !this.allSelected();
});
```

Still `false` at the cap (where `allSelected` is `true`), and `true` for any partial selection regardless of where the rows sit in the list.

</details>

