inline.body:
🎨 **SUGGESTED**: Asserting on raw template text passes on any formatting change and never exercises the binding.

<details>
<summary>Details and fix</summary>

`toContain('(clear)="service.clearSelection()"')` fails if Prettier ever rewraps the attribute or someone writes `service.clearSelection( )`, and passes even if `clearSelection` is renamed on the service — nothing type-checks the string.

The stories in this PR already solve the missing-outlet problem in ~8 lines (`StoryLayoutFooterComponent` in `vault-items-table.stories.ts`). Same idea here turns this into a behavioral test:

```ts
@Component({
  template: `<ng-template [cdkPortalOutlet]="portal()"></ng-template>`,
  imports: [PortalModule],
})
class FooterOutletComponent {
  protected readonly portal = inject(LayoutFooterService).portal;
}
```

Render it alongside the component, click the bar's Clear button, and assert `clearSpy` was called. That covers the same regression (`selection.clear()` leaving the bar up once a source is registered) without depending on how the template happens to be formatted.
</details>

